  "generated_description": "<div class=\"mountain-description prose prose-stone max-w-none\">\n  <p><strong>Corn Hill</strong> rises to 1,194 feet in Iowa.</p>\n  <h3>When to Go</h3><p>Spring through fall is the main season. Conditions change fast in the shoulder months \u2014 check a point forecast for the summit, not the nearest town, before you commit.</p>\n  <h3>Know Before You Go</h3><p>Download the GPX track from this page before you go \u2014 cell coverage is unreliable in the mountains and a saved route works offline in any GPS app. Conditions change: verify current access, closures and weather with the official land manager before you go. Trail data is sourced from OpenStreetMap contributors (ODbL).</p>\n  <p>Looking to link objectives or plan a weekend? Nearby summits include Sugar Loaf, Steamboat Rock and Mount Hosmer \u2014 each has its own guide on this site.</p>\n</div>",
